hdw4s (1.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  An account now has one desktop per machine. Instance names of the form
  "<user>:<session>", which gave one account a second concurrent desktop on the
  same machine, are no longer created.

  Nothing is removed from a machine by this upgrade. An instance enabled by an
  earlier version keeps running, keeps its slot and keeps its port, and
  "hdw4s list" reports it with the state "legacy" so it can be found. Every
  command refuses that name except "hdw4s release", which stops the session
  first, so retiring one is a single command:

      hdw4s release alice:2

  You do not have to. A legacy instance that is left alone goes on working.

  One account with a desktop on several machines, against one home directory,
  is a different arrangement, is unaffected, and remains what
  HDW4S_ISOLATION=profile exists for.

 -- Markus Gutschke <gutschke@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:00:00 -0700

